# Row-aware 3-way merge for the shared JSON registers.
#
# MEASURED, main @1b82ab7: these five files re-conflict every sibling PR, and the
# dominant mechanism is a shared header scalar rather than the rows —
# 74% of MANAGER-CHECKLIST.json conflict pairs and 67% of OPEN-PRS.json ones have
# BOTH sides bumping the same `updated_at`/`as_of` line. PR #10815's entire
# conflict was that one line.
#
# ⚠️ A MERGE DRIVER IS CLIENT-SIDE. Git runs it on `git merge` / `git rebase`
# LOCALLY, and ONLY after `scripts/ops/install_merge_driver.sh` has registered it
# in this clone's git config. GitHub's servers do NOT run custom merge drivers, so
# this does NOT make a `mergeable_state: dirty` PR auto-mergeable on GitHub — it
# removes the cost of resolving the conflict by hand, which is the measured
# consumer of manager time. Saying otherwise would be claiming a fix that is not
# there.
#
# The driver REFUSES (exit 1, markers left) on divergent same-id adds or edits and
# on delete-vs-edit. It never picks a winner. See scripts/ops/merge_json_register.py.
#
# ⚠️ SHIPPING IT IS NOT ARMING IT, AND FOR THE FIRST DAY NOBODY WAS ARMED. Measured
# 2026-09-03 (MI-94): `git config --get merge.jsonregister.driver` was EMPTY in a
# fresh clone, and nothing in the SessionStart hook, any skill, or CI ran the
# installer — so every session container merged these files the old way. Two
# sibling branches each appending one row conflicted in 4 of 4 registers un-armed
# and 0 of 3 armed. `scripts/ops/manager_preflight.py`'s `merge_driver` check now
# FAILS an un-armed clone and names the one-line remedy, so the gap is visible at
# the moment it costs something rather than after.
#
# ⚠️ AND THE DRIVER IS ONLY HALF THE PROBLEM. It resolves the TEXTUAL collision; it
# cannot see a SEMANTIC one — a branch filing new work under an id `main` already
# gave to something else is, to git, one changed value at one key, so the merge
# DELETES the existing row and reports success. `scripts/ci/check_register_ids.py`
# (`register-id-guard`) is that half, and it runs on every PR.

docs/claude/health-review-backlog.json      merge=jsonregister
docs/claude/OPEN-ITEMS.json                 merge=jsonregister
docs/claude/work/MANAGER-CHECKLIST.json     merge=jsonregister
docs/claude/work/SESSIONS.json              merge=jsonregister
docs/claude/work/OPEN-PRS.json              merge=jsonregister
